4.1 Conclusions
For Ignacio (The Analytical/Strategic)
Subject: Initial Phase Conclusion: Infrastructure in Production and Strategic Pivot to Security (Activity 5)

The Initial Development Phase of EcoFinder has concluded successfully, establishing a robust technical foundation. The most critical achievement is the implementation of real-time data persistence using PostgreSQL, ensuring the integrity and immediacy of the Dynamic Map (Leaflet.js). Furthermore, the completion of the Rewards Catalog fully validates our core value proposition.

However, this progress has revealed an immediate strategic need to reprioritize resources towards security. The vulnerability of user point balances and transactional integrity demands that we advance and prioritize Activity 5: PostgreSQL Security Policies/Rules. This pivot is paramount to ensure the project meets the highest quality and security indicators required by the discipline. In short: Infrastructure OK, the focus is now on hardening system integrity.

For Elías (The Direct/Executive)
Subject: EcoFinder: Infrastructure Complete. CRITICAL Next Step: Security (PostgreSQL Rules).

EcoFinder’s core infrastructure stage is completed.

Key Achievement: PostgreSQL integration ensures our recycling map is always up-to-date in real time.

Value Confirmed: The Rewards Catalog interface is ready, validating the project's core.

However, infrastructure success mandates an immediate priority shift. Security is now the weak spot. We must Pivot: Move all available resources to Activity 5 (PostgreSQL Security Policies/Rules). This is fundamental for protecting user points and ensuring transactional integrity, a non-negotiable quality requirement. The system is working; we must now secure it.

